# <type>(<scope>): <description>
#
# Conventional Commits (https://www.conventionalcommits.org).
# type: lowercase, one of
#   feat     new behavior
#   fix      broken behavior made right
#   docs     documentation only
#   style    formatting only, no logic change
#   refactor same behavior, different code
#   perf     faster or lighter
#   test     tests only
#   chore    tooling, config, dependencies
#   ci       CI/CD only
# scope: optional, the area touched (e.g. zsh, git-wt, lazygit)
# description: English, lowercase imperative ("add", not "Add" / "added"),
#   72 characters max, no trailing period
#
# Body (optional, after a blank line): 1-3 sentences on what changed and why,
#   one paragraph per line (do not hard-wrap).
# Footer: "Fixes #123" when an issue applies.
